<title>BRAZIL: Brazil shipping bill vote delayed in lower house.</title>
<headline>Brazil shipping bill vote delayed in lower house.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bill regulating inland and coastal shipping, which prompted portworkers to go on strike Tuesday, will be put to a vote on Wednesday and not Tuesday as previously expected, the deputy who wrote the bill said.</p>
<p>Dep. Jose Carlos Aleluia said the lower house would only vote on the bill Wednesday to allow more time for last-minute changes to its text.</p>
<p>Brazilian portworker unions said earlier on Tuesday they would continue their 24-hour strike into Wednesday if the voting was delayed. The unions say the bill tramples on worker rights.</p>
<p>-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358</p>
